--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY ARITHMETIC (reproduced EXACTLY from the web source — value parity, NOT a "corrected" version)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  battery (gauge) = value = batteryLevel ?? 0 ; centre = fmtNumber(value, 0) [RadialGauge decimals 0]
  battery (hero)  = batteryLevel != null ? fmtNumber(batteryLevel, 0) : '—' [WidgetBigNumber nullDisplay]
  batteryColor    = > 50 green · > 20 amber · else red ; null → grey track  [getBatteryColor]
  range           = convertDistanceFromSI(range_km * 1000, unit) then fmtNumber(·, 0)
                    [ /1000 km · /1609.344 mi · /0.3048 ft ]  ; '—' when range_km null
  cabin temp      = convertTempFromSI(inside_temp_c, unit) then fmtNumber(·, 0)
                    [ °C pass-through · °F = c*9/5+32 ]       ; '—' when inside_temp_c null
  state (compact) = capitalize(state) + FSM badgeDot tone (online=success · driving/parked/updating=info ·
                    charging=warning · asleep=neutral · offline=danger)        [StatusBadge]
  state (hero)    = raw state + badge tone (online→success · asleep→neutral · else→warning) [web ternary]
  lock            = is_locked == true → Locked/success · false → Unlocked/warning · null → '—'
  last seen       = relative (RelativeDateTimeFormatter) ; '—' when null/invalid   [TimeStamp]
  charging        = complication.charging → compact "⚡ Charging"
  isCompact       = size.cols <= 1

States reproduced (every one renders — no hidden surfaces), each with a #if DEBUG preview:
  loading (skeleton chrome) · empty ("No watch data") · error (retry) · stale (chip + banner +
  auto-refresh) · offline (cached glance + banner/chip) · content (compact watch-face / standard grid).

